        "type": "paragraph",
        "html": "The science fair had been in the east gym, which always smelled of varnish and oranges because the janitor believed in oranges. Ivo's board had taken him eleven months: moth wings pinned in a grid, each vein drawn again by hand, and in the corner a rubbing he had made from a stone fragment in the Harrowgate museum, an inscription no one at St. Briony was meant to care about. He had cared about it with the helpless greed of a person who had finally found a door that opened inward.",
